describes --describes[1.0]--> the meaning of a relation
invariant --describes[1.0]--> a rule this repository holds
topic --describes[1.0]--> which index section an invariant belongs to
governs --describes[1.0]--> path whose edit the invariant constrains
located --describes[1.0]--> evidence anchor for the construct
located_in --describes[1.0]--> file holding the anchor
enforced_by --describes[1.0]--> check that fails when invariant is violated
enforced_by_prefix --describes[1.0]--> greppable prefix of a long check name
enforced_in --describes[1.0]--> file holding the named check
prose_in --describes[1.0]--> document carrying the full argument
rationale --describes[1.0]--> why the invariant exists
row --describes[1.0]--> diagnostics row identifier the invariant produces
host_path --describes[1.0]--> a path on a machine the rule fixes
figure --describes[1.0]--> a number or version the rule states
names --describes[1.0]--> an identifier the rule names
registration_point --describes[1.0]--> hand maintained list an addition must join
register_in --describes[1.0]--> file holding the registration list
bug --describes[1.0]--> a known defect recorded in the index
symptom --describes[1.0]--> how the bug presents itself
workaround --describes[1.0]--> what to do about the bug
counterexample --describes[1.0]--> claim asserted against current behaviour
home --describes[1.0]--> file holding a counterexample probe
status --describes[1.0]--> lifecycle state of a counterexample
dead_end --describes[1.0]--> design searched and ruled out
revived_by --describes[1.0]--> trigger that reopens a parked design
change_status --describes[1.0]--> landed or open or parked or struck
prior_art --describes[1.0]--> external design this layer already is
decision --describes[1.0]--> a choice this repository took
stale_anchor --describes[1.0]--> a path the index names unresolved
index_drift --describes[1.0]--> the index states what the tree contradicts
index_line --describes[1.0]--> where the index states it
index_says --describes[1.0]--> the value the index states
tree_says --describes[1.0]--> the value the tree holds
closed_by --describes[1.0]--> the change that closes this finding
owns_capability --describes[1.0]--> capability delta the change may write
located_line --describes[1.0]--> the line an anchor names
